      "small_logo_thumb_url": "https://bookface-images.s3.amazonaws.com/small_logos/a310be93d13c548ee674125ec85077cd90ed1e23.png",
      "website": "https://ploverlabs.ai/",
      "all_locations": "San Francisco, CA, USA",
      "long_description": "Plover Labs is building toward a future where AI agents write, ship, and maintain most of a company's software. We make it possible for agents to own real engineering roles, not just suggest code for someone else to approve.\r\n\r\nCoding models keep getting more capable, but enterprise adoption lags behind AI-native startups because enterprises don't yet trust agent output. Each codebase has conventions, history, and failure modes that a general-purpose model doesn't know. We learn those continuously from the code, how the team works, and the mistakes agents make. Then we fix the codebase and add merge gates that use deterministic verifiers instead of another model's judgment, so the same mistake can't ship twice. As the gates build up, agents can be trusted with more of the work.\r\n\r\nWe have five-figure monthly contracts with Series C companies Envoy and Fieldguide. At Fieldguide, we tripled PRs per engineer in one quarter, with the same headcount and PR size.",
      "one_liner": "Enable enterprises to ship agent code without human review",
      "team_size": 2,
